  "verdict": "The depot preference is a calibration problem and is fixed by a constant (stage A): one scalar, default 0, turns 0.798 held-out completion into 0.892 with no retraining and leaves the old behaviour bit-for-bit when unset. The heuristic residual is still the best arm (0.911) and the coalition term adds nothing measurable (0.916, +3 targets of 588 over rs0.25, identical on 99.94% of development decisions), because a candidate robot's own belief almost never shows a capability gap it could fill -- the gap that kills the remaining 50 targets is only visible across robots, and the per-pair bias interface cannot convene a group.",
